Z||000000||ds21||05-18-2001||12:25 PM||||Hello all, I just got an 85GT and needed some parts and was wondering where are some places to get parts at a good price. First things first... ball joints need them, also if I understand you need to replace the lower A-arm as opossed to just the ball joint? And AirCond... what if any thing special do you need to do to convert Air to a134? how hard is it to do, I've never done AirCond before. Thank you!!!||||reg||12
Z||000001||Taijiguy||05-18-2001||01:23 PM||||Any decent auto parts place will have major repair and tune-up parts. Ball joints included. You don't have to replace the entire lower control arm to replace the ball joint. You will have to drill out the existing rivets (if the joints are original) the new ball joint will come with bolts and locking nuts. For other items like, performance and custom items, you can get them from any number of places, many of whom have members on this forum. Also post wants to "The Mall"...many people here have several Fieros that they use for parts, and will gladly sell you items at a generally reasonable price.<BR>Welcome to the asylum... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||84Bill||05-18-2001||01:33 PM||||Welcome to the forum!<BR>Click on the search link below and search the tech section there was a recent post on that.||||reg||14
Z||000003||tgowens||05-18-2001||04:29 PM||||Cliff has included a "Fiero Parts Vendors" link on here - scroll to the bottom of this page and you will see the link -- hope this helps..<P>------------------<BR>My Fiero Web Site.....<BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tgowens.gif">              </A><P>87 GT - 2.8L Gold automatic<BR>87 GT - 2.8L Blue automatic<BR>87 GT - 3.4L Blue 5-speed Getrag<BR>87 GT - 2.8L Med. Red Met. 5-speed Getrag<BR>88 Coupe - 2.5L Red automatic||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||05-18-2001||05:33 PM||||You can buy a kit for around $35 to change over. I wouldnt change from R12 myself. Ive had cars with both and R12 cools better than 134. Some others will differ with me, but thats my own experience. They will work changed over but there is a lot more that should be changed to work at its best. I think compressors are different, all the seals internally are not compatable, and you cant mix the two. My lumina vans air is cool but def not cold and its just been serviced. My Fiero with R12 will keep a soda cold in front of the vent.||||reg||1
