Z||000006||Bob Englert||05-18-2001||09:35 PM||||Lower ball joints are available from AutoZone for about $16 each.  You do not need to replace the entire control arm, but you will probably have to remove it to get the old ball joint pressed out and the new one pressed in.  Removing and replacing the front springs are a challenge.<P>First thing, get a Haynes manual and keep an eye out for a factory (Helms) manual on eBay for your model year.  Very helpful.  I wouldn't try half the repairs I have make without the manuals.  <P>If you do replace the lower ball joints, do it right and rebuilt the entire front suspension (upper ball joints, lower ball joints, upper and lower control arm bushings, outer tie rod ends, etc).  It is much easier to do at once when you are taking things apart.  The difference in how the car will feel is amazing.<P>Good luck, and welcome!<P>P.S.  Update your profile so we know where you are from.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
